NV12 + MUTABLE_FORMAT: do not drop the image to linear, drop only UBWC

tu_image.cc: in the planar NV12 branch, images with
VK_IMAGE_CREATE_MUTABLE_FORMAT_BIT got two restrictions at once:

    ubwc_enabled = false;
    force_linear_tile = true;

The first is necessary and sufficient. The second is redundant, and
because of it NV12 + MUTABLE + SPARSE_RESIDENTCY could not be created
at all: patch 0004 refuses creation when tile_mode != TILE6_3, because
sparse-block addressing describes a tiled layout, and a linear sparse
image silently reads the wrong addresses.

Why the layout does not change. tu_image_view_init reinterprets the
same plane 0 as Y8/R8: the comment in the code calls this exactly a
difference in compression ("the 0'th plane of this format has a
different UBWC compression"), i.e. the reinterpretation is treated as
identical in layout. And the layout is built by exactly the same
format: tu6_plane_format() returns PIPE_FORMAT_Y8_UNORM for plane 0,
and that same value goes into tu_image_init. The base format of plane 1
also matches (R8_UNORM / PIPE_FORMAT_R8_UNORM). So only what the data
is compressed with changes, not the geometry of the planes, and a
separate tiling prohibition is unnecessary.

What this gives, besides removing the rejection:

 - NV12 + MUTABLE stops being linear. For video this is a common
   configuration, and the demotion to linear costs bandwidth and
   tiling.
 - The only path reachable from vkd3d into the 0004 rejection is
   removed, so patching vkd3d is not required.
 - The change is not in a gen2 quirk but in common code: the UBWC
   refusal stays (that was the point of the branch), only tiling
   changes. The effect is the same on gen2/g3/a8xx, and 0004 keeps
   working for all other paths into a linear sparse image.

Verified by measurement, probe N in tests/rp6-vkd3d-sparse-test.c:

    | build                     | N2: NV12+MUTABLE+SPARSE |
    |---------------------------|-------------------------|
    | stock                     | SUCCESS                 |
    | 0004-0008                  | FEATURE_NOT_PRESENT     |
    | 0004-0008 + this patch    | SUCCESS                 |

The signal is independent of size computation: the 0004 gate in
tu_image.cc refuses exactly when tile_mode != TILE6_3, so SUCCESS means
TILE6_3 directly.

Planar layout measurements (probe W) and memreq are given in
docs/analysis.md, section 18.

Upstream-worthiness: the change removes an unnecessary demotion and
adds no chip checks, so it is an upstream candidate as a separate
tu_image.cc fix.
Relations: builds on 0004 - it removes the only path reachable from
vkd3d into the rejection that patch introduces. Applies standalone even
without 0004.

